  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Tourism businessman Costakis Loizou was only 25 when he urged his father to bid for the Ledra Palace hotel. His father initially dismissed the suggestion as unrealistic: the family then owned a much smaller hotel in Nicosia. He nevertheless investigated the opportunity and completed the purchase, without first telling his son.\n\nLoizou's subsequent expansion into cruising offered holidaymakers in Cyprus short excursions to Egypt and Israel. The group introduced trips lasting one to three days, allowing visitors to add neighbouring countries to their island holiday. Its entry into ship ownership followed earlier work representing passenger vessels, and made these short international journeys part of the wider holiday offering.",
    "html": "<p>Tourism businessman Costakis Loizou was only 25 when he urged his father to bid for the Ledra Palace hotel. His father initially dismissed the suggestion as unrealistic: the family then owned a much smaller hotel in Nicosia. He nevertheless investigated the opportunity and completed the purchase, without first telling his son.</p>\r\n<p>Loizou's subsequent expansion into cruising offered holidaymakers in Cyprus short excursions to Egypt and Israel. The group introduced trips lasting one to three days, allowing visitors to add neighbouring countries to their island holiday. Its entry into ship ownership followed earlier work representing passenger vessels, and made these short international journeys part of the wider holiday offering.</p>\r\n",
